comment.body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Reorder imports to follow the coding guidelines.**

Imports should be ordered: std, external crates, then `crate::`/`super::`/`self::`. Currently `crate::` imports appear before external crate imports.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-use crate::api::relays::Relay;
-use crate::api::wn;
-use crate::api::{ApiError, metadata::FlutterMetadata};
-use crate::frb_generated::StreamSink;
 use chrono::{DateTime, Utc};
 use flutter_rust_bridge::frb;
 use nostr_sdk::prelude::*;
 use whitenoise::{
     KeyPackageStatus as WhitenoiseKeyPackageStatus, RelayType, User as WhitenoiseUser,
     UserUpdate as WhitenoiseUserUpdate, UserUpdateTrigger as WhitenoiseUserUpdateTrigger,
     Whitenoise,
 };
+
+use crate::api::relays::Relay;
+use crate::api::wn;
+use crate::api::{ApiError, metadata::FlutterMetadata};
+use crate::frb_generated::StreamSink;
```
</details>

As per coding guidelines: place import statements at the top of scope in order: std, external crates, `mod` declarations, `crate::`/`super::`/`self::`.

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@crates/whitenoise-frb/src/api/users.rs` around lines 1 - 12, Reorder the use
statements so external crates come before crate-local imports: move uses of
chrono::{DateTime, Utc}, flutter_rust_bridge::frb, nostr_sdk::prelude::*, and
whitenoise::{...} to appear above any crate::... imports; then place
crate::api::relays::Relay, crate::api::wn, crate::api::{ApiError,
metadata::FlutterMetadata}, and crate::frb_generated::StreamSink after the
externals. Keep each use group together (external crates grouped, then crate::
group) and preserve the specific symbols like Relay, ApiError, FlutterMetadata,
StreamSink, WhitenoiseUser, WhitenoiseUserUpdateTrigger, etc., so callers such
as the functions referencing these names are unaffected.
```

</details>

